18016 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186517517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518016 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5bd3a5dd-dd4c-547c-b5d1-8d0a45894fb2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518141 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518141 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163495" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518141 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518141 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/85/8524ffd2ff653703bd6fcfa2b44d36821aeb34877d58bbc6df388497cac8e07d.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $x$-axis and the lines $y=2x$ and $y=4-2x$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{x}{2}.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518141 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5810c34a-c4d1-5c91-ad48-b47e68d3d961" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518141 #edb/ref 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type II region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{y}{2}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/29/293f8454cdda5897de111d6444baa4674eccf28a36e2053f3f2cb71f948e07fe.png)\n\n  \n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{2-y/2}\\frac{x}{2}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{2-y/2}x(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4y+4)[{\\int }_{y/2}^{2-y/2}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4y+4){[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=y/2}^{x=2-y/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4y+4)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[{(2-\\frac{y}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{y}{2})}^{2}]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4y+4)(4-2y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}-2{y}^{3}+12{y}^{2}-24y+16\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}+4{y}^{3}-12{y}^{2}+16y]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(-8+32-48+32) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518195 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518195 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163668" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518195 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518195 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/de/de1ac9ccf84134913bbf8847ea9795a1ec83084602db705c8bef723897e7bd92.png)\n\nA triangular plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant enclosed between the axes and the line $y=1-x.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518195 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c9bc333f-6b0c-5f6d-9c9d-d8671bcc2662" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518195 #edb/ref 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/a0/a092d57585bd7b2803473c30328dd72f82a6611d8398de821099db72e2ed3621.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $x=3$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-3|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k|x|=kx,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}kx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{[y]}_{0}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}x(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}x-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=kx=6Mx.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}6Mx\\,|x-3{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}6Mx(x-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+9x)[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+9x){[y]}_{0}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+9x)(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-{x}^{4}+7{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+9x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6M{[-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{7}{4}{x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =6M[-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{7}{4}-5+\\frac{9}{2}-0] \\\\  & =6M[\\frac{21}{20}] \\\\  & =\\frac{63M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518221 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518221 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163644" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518221 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518221 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/16/1664a86a1fee25cccbb710ad4335e4d69b36c24d64c95ae7bff9e54d2ac3a6b6.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $x=\\sqrt{2y}$ and $x=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\frac{4}{3},$ find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518221 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f58ffe9b-0496-58b1-afb0-490bd07410f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518221 #edb/ref 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type II region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2y}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/d9/d9c529fe2d238a3d6ac4e20cfcd571f980c28a4eb2c13497fab3ccb0d15ac6eb.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{3M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}\\frac{3M}{4}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-2)^{2}[x]_{x={y}^{2}/2}^{x=\\sqrt{2y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-2)^{2}(\\sqrt{2y}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\sqrt{2}{y}^{5/2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}-4\\sqrt{2}{y}^{3/2}+2{y}^{3}+4\\sqrt{2}{y}^{1/2}-2{y}^{2})\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{[\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}{y}^{7/2}}{7}-\\frac{{y}^{5}}{10}-\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}{y}^{5/2}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}+\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}{y}^{3/2}}{3}-\\frac{2{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}(\\frac{32}{7}-\\frac{32}{10}-\\frac{64}{5}+8+\\frac{32}{3}-\\frac{16}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}(\\frac{40}{21}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10M}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518248 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186518295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518248 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "43368631-ebb7-5e59-8710-99f4db8da10e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518248 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186284385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518252 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "49428a33-5d98-5966-ad50-cdf5ae5c8855" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518252 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186518195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518271 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186518248 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518271 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "91404c15-d1ad-50fd-86be-ced9527f549e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518271 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186281671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518285 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186518271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518285 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b4eb2f43-d2cd-51a1-99f9-5fba6e8ad21f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518285 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186518141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518295 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186518252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518295 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ca887437-9db2-5a07-9af6-a9d5c2c7ebbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518295 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186518221 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
